cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this testbed or its findings, please cite it as below."
title: "candidate-language-testbed: a synthetic-ground-truth testbed for text-based ideology measurement"
authors:
  - family-names: Ripper
    given-names: Ryan
type: software
date-released: "2026-08-18"
year: 2026
url: "https://github.com/ryanripper/candidate-language-testbed"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ryanripper/candidate-language-testbed"
abstract: >-
  A synthetic corpus of 104,601 tweets from 910 fictional 2022-cycle
  candidates with planted ideological ground truth, plus a blind
  seal/preregister/unseal harness, used to measure how well six families of
  text-based instruments recover planted ideology - and whether their
  failures are detectable without the answer key.
keywords:
  - ideal point estimation
  - text as data
  - political methodology
  - synthetic data
  - embeddings
  - topic models
